WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:09.400
With old St. Nick just around the corner, workers at Shelton, Washington put in long

00:09.400 --> 00:15.720
hours to ensure early arrival of selected Yuletide trees to all parts of the country.

00:15.720 --> 00:23.440
Every branch bears the Christmas spirit.

00:23.440 --> 00:28.080
At Seattle's Naval Air Station, a special load of Christmas cheer is put aboard a plane

00:28.080 --> 00:32.680
bound for various points in the icy northern wastes where our troops still protect our

00:32.680 --> 00:34.280
arctic outposts.

00:34.280 --> 00:39.880
Merry Christmas, Joe.

00:39.880 --> 00:44.280
All over the nation, eager shoppers parade before store windows packed with bright and

00:44.280 --> 00:48.360
shining presents for all the family, especially the youngsters.

00:48.360 --> 00:52.160
And it's a big problem to make a selection without breaking Santa.

00:52.160 --> 00:57.080
Pretty little girls and big beautiful dolls and happy tots galloping hobby horses are

00:57.080 --> 01:04.400
found at every toy department.

01:04.400 --> 01:08.280
A handful of enticing puppetry brings a glow of anticipation.

01:08.280 --> 01:12.840
And if you want father's heart to beat faster on Christmas morning, have Chris Kringle deliver

01:12.840 --> 01:21.160
a load of these streamliners to the children.

01:21.160 --> 01:28.200
If the limited is held up at the bridge, well, presto, and the Christmas flyer gets the green

01:28.200 --> 01:33.600
light.

01:33.600 --> 01:36.120
Everybody's friend has something for everyone.

01:36.120 --> 01:51.760
If you know of someone he might miss, open up your heart and have a Merry Christmas.

01:51.760 --> 01:57.180
I have taken over the duties of the Chief of Staff of the Army from a great predecessor.

01:57.180 --> 02:00.720
And of course, I'm honored by the selection.

02:00.720 --> 02:06.040
But I'm keenly aware that I've taken up this duty at a critical time in the affairs of

02:06.040 --> 02:08.600
the nation and of the Army.

02:08.600 --> 02:13.840
To win the war, you raised the greatest army in our history.

02:13.840 --> 02:19.400
We are now engaged in tearing down that army at an unprecedented rate.

02:19.400 --> 02:25.200
At the same time, we have commitments in foreign lands, commitments which require military

02:25.200 --> 02:26.800
strength.

02:26.800 --> 02:31.680
Those commitments were made in good faith to help solidify the peace that has been so

02:31.680 --> 02:34.240
dearly won.

02:34.240 --> 02:38.600
Very soon, those two processes will clash.

02:38.600 --> 02:43.680
This is your army, and it is your decision as to which course we shall follow.

02:43.680 --> 02:49.040
The decision once made, it is the duty of the War Department to carry it out.

02:49.040 --> 02:59.240
For my part, I hope that we secure that peace.

02:59.240 --> 03:04.040
One family in a Southern California community is proud today, and that's the Masudas whose

03:04.040 --> 03:09.480
Japanese-American son died heroically during the terrific battle for Cassino, Italy.

03:09.480 --> 03:14.280
Sergeant Masuda was sighted for the Distinguished Service Cross two weeks before he was killed.

03:14.280 --> 03:18.480
After a flight from Washington, General Stilwell presents the medal posthumously to the sergeant's

03:18.480 --> 03:20.520
sister.

03:20.520 --> 03:26.960
A brave American soldier is remembered, and his loyal family is an honor to the country

03:26.960 --> 03:36.960
for which he died.

03:36.960 --> 03:42.040
Surrounded by youthful members of his flock, Archbishop Spellman of New York opens a nationwide

03:42.040 --> 03:49.240
campaign to collect canned supplies for war-devastated people of all faiths.

03:49.240 --> 03:56.080
These boys and girls are actively engaged in a campaign for canned goods that will begin

03:56.080 --> 03:59.760
throughout the United States this coming week.

03:59.760 --> 04:07.480
And these boys and girls, by their gifts are these canned goods, hope to heal and strengthen

04:07.480 --> 04:14.640
the wasted and worn bodies of other boys and girls throughout the world who are suffering

04:14.640 --> 04:16.720
and starving.

04:16.720 --> 04:24.040
And during this week, every Catholic parish in the United States, 15,000 of them, will

04:24.040 --> 04:31.240
act as a receiving station for canned goods to help the poor and the suffering children

04:31.240 --> 04:42.880
and the people throughout the world without discrimination of race, creed, or color.

04:42.880 --> 04:47.880
Arriving at Washington, D.C., the Mixmaster, piloted by Lieutenant Colonel H.E.

04:47.880 --> 04:52.600
Warden, completes a record-breaking nonstop flight from Long Beach, California.

04:52.600 --> 04:58.040
Co-pilot Captain Glenn Edwards shared the job on the swift flight of five hours, 17

04:58.040 --> 05:01.840
minutes, topping the former unofficial mark of six hours from Seattle.

05:01.840 --> 05:06.160
The Speedy Douglas bomber gets her nickname from her radical tail propellers, which sing

05:06.160 --> 05:09.240
a mighty song.

05:09.240 --> 05:13.760
Not to be outdone in design, the Navy displays its newest, the Boeing Tandem Prop fighter

05:13.760 --> 05:14.760
plane.

05:14.760 --> 05:19.720
The single 3,600 horsepower engine drives her two propellers in opposite directions.

05:19.720 --> 05:30.440
The Navy says she'll do better than 450 miles per hour.

05:30.440 --> 05:40.640
The versatile craft can be used as a fighter, torpedo plane, bomber, attack plane, or interceptor.

05:40.640 --> 05:53.800
A real addition to our protective air forces.

